    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1154-a1">

                <pb facs="1004" n="900" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg900"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Minister to
                            Mexico to the American Charge’
                            d’Affaires.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spanish Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-10-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 16, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Colleague</hi>: All the informations
                    available from different sources and places agree in recognizing that the
                    ill-will and propaganda against the Spaniards comes from certain revolutionary
                    elements, and perhaps now in the first place from Don Venustiano Carranza and
                    his brother Jesús, who, I am told, have issued special orders to that effect in
                    the campaign against Torreón.</p>
                <p>I renew [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">B. J. de Cologán</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
